      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For anyone who can make a difference, the issue described can be easily replicated with any avatar using the default locomotion controller in full body and simply jumping. Ideally, there would be a solution for not only jumping and falling, but also landing. Specifically in regard to the behavior itself, it would be best that fbt users still have full control when falling straight down, and only lose control of their lower body (hips and legs) when moving in a certain direction.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-08T13:58:02.374Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Jumping causes the FBT pose to be overwritten by an animation. Even when having copied your example locomotion and having either removed the fall&jump logic or added impossible conditions towards the execution of it, it still forces some kind of default stance onto the avatar hips down. It also seems to cause problems in maps where is some sort of swimming mechanic, because the avatar gets stuck in falling animation (default locomotion and the one with removed jumping/falling logic).\nPerfect would be behavior like 2.0 avatars, only jumping animation while running/walking. near standstill jumps/falling should not trigger an animation during fbt.\nBesides: turning off 6 point locomotion helps for jump and fall, but for some reason \"landing\" still sometimes triggers an animation.\nEdit:\nMaybe an option like \"disable VelocityY conditions for 6 point tracking\" in  would be a desired result. It could be an additional condition for the controllers to check, so one could decide for each avatar to use jumping/falling animations or not rather easily.",
